PARITY (web source reproduced end-to-end)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - Data source (web `useTranslation`; the controlled `values: Record<AiFeatureId, boolean>` +
    `onToggle(id, value)` fed by the settings-form parent): bound through the P1/S8 seam
    AIFeatureToggleSource → AIFeatureToggleListModel. The view never issues HTTP; the source resolves the
    opt-in values + pushes coalesced updates, and a flip persists through `setEnabled` (web `onToggle`).
  - Composition (web `<section rounded-md border p-4 space-y-2 aria-label={legend}>` > `<Subhead>`legend
    + `AI_FEATURE_IDS.map(...)` of `<div>` label + `<Caption>` + `<Toggle>`):
      • <section> border    -> bordered rounded container (TSRadius.md + Color.TS.border), wrapped in
                               TSFadeIn(delay 0.1); aria-label -> accessibilityLabel = legend.
      • <Subhead> legend    -> uppercase-weight Subhead (Font.TS.bodySm semibold textSecondary),
                               web t('ai.settings.feature.legend','Per-feature opt-in (all default off)').
      • per-feature rows    -> AIFeatureRegistry.all (= AI_FEATURE_IDS, 57, same order) each:
          - label   -> t('ai.settings.feature.<id>.label', meta.name)        (bodySm medium textPrimary).
          - desc    -> t('ai.settings.feature.<id>.description', meta.description) (caption textMuted).
          - Toggle  -> Toggle(.switch).tint(accent), checked = Boolean(values[id]) (absent ⇒ off),
                       onChange -> model.toggle(id,next) -> source.setEnabled (optimistic + persist).
  - i18n: the legend key + all 57 label keys + all 57 description keys mirror the web
    t('ai.settings.feature.*') calls; the long meta.description blurbs ship verbatim in the .strings
    catalogue (NOT as oversized Swift literals), pinned non-empty by the catalogue test.
  - States (every one renders; web leaf is controlled-only, native owns the lifecycle like AISettings):
      loading -> skeleton rows; empty -> friendly empty state (no settings record); error -> retryable
      QueryError peer; data -> the toggle list; stale/offline -> freshness chip + cached banner + one-shot
      stale auto-refresh.
  - a11y: each switch is the interactive element with accessibilityLabel = feature name (web
    aria-label={label}) + the description as its hint + native on/off value; decorative label/description
    text hidden from VoiceOver to avoid duplication. Projection carries a combined VoiceOver summary.
  - Telemetry: model.start() emits the P1/S11 `view.opened` event with slug "AIFeatureToggleList" exactly
    once (asserted).

